  "description": "The schema exposes a global exit-code taxonomy but not the command outcomes that produce each code. Documentation must currently cite runtime classification and direct exits instead of a maintained projection.\n\nSource: `crates/jit/src/schema.rs:520-556`; `crates/jit/src/main.rs:33-247`; `crates/jit/src/output_macros.rs:112-121`; `dev/archive/2d109173-docs-exhaustive-audit/2d109173-plan.md:384-403`.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: A discoverable generated surface identifies per-command or per-command-family exit codes, including exceptions to the global taxonomy.\n- [hard] REQ-02: The projection derives from or is mechanically verified against runtime classification and dispatch sources.\n- [hard] REQ-03: Documentation consuming the new surface does not hand-copy per-command exit-code tables.",
